    "title": "Public Safety Alert canceled after missing 9-year-old boy found - NewsBreak",
    "text": "UPDATE: Fort Wayne dispatchers confirmed the boy has been found. FORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) — Fort Wayne police are searching for a missing 9-year-old boy last seen near Waynedale. The boy, identified as Titus Harman, was last seen in the area of Sandpoint and Tyrone roads, according to a Public Safety Alert. Police described Titus as white and last wearing a red and camo hoodie with black sweatpants. Anyone with information regarding Titus’ whereabouts should contact the Fort Wayne Police Department at 260-427-1222. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
